# Clock Fix Pro

**Batch-change the recording date and time of your video clips.**
Free desktop app for Windows 10 and 11.

Download → [**Latest release**](../../releases/latest)

---

## The problem

You shot with several cameras. One of them had the wrong clock — off by
three hours, or still on last year's date because the battery died.

Now the files are dated at a moment that never happened. Your editor
sorts them by that date, so the takes land all over the place and
automatic sync has nothing to work with.

## What it does

Clock Fix Pro rewrites the recording date and time stored **inside** your
clips, in batches, before you bring them into an editor.

Not the file creation date Windows shows — that one changes on its own
every time you copy a folder. It writes the internal metadata your editor
actually reads: `QuickTime:CreateDate`, `MediaCreateDate` and the
matching EXIF tags.

- **Two ways to fix it.** Set one exact date and time for the whole
  batch, or add and subtract time from whatever each clip already had.
  The second is what repairs a clock that ran three hours behind without
  losing the gaps between takes.
- **No re-encoding.** Only the metadata is touched. Picture and audio
  stay exactly as they were, bit for bit, and the job takes seconds.
- **You see it before it happens.** Every row shows its current date and
  the one it will get.
- **With a way back.** It keeps a backup of every clip and one button
  undoes the whole batch. It can also write the corrected copies to a
  separate folder and never touch your originals.
- **Nothing leaves your computer.** No uploads, no account, no telemetry.

## Free and Pro

The free version fixes dates and times, with **no limit on how many
clips**. No quotas, no expiry, no account.

Pro adds the rest of the metadata a working shoot needs:

| | Free | Pro |
|---|---|---|
| Recording date and time | ✅ | ✅ |
| Clips per batch | unlimited | unlimited |
| Backup copies and undo | ✅ | ✅ |
| Time zone | | ✅ |
| Camera make and model | | ✅ |
| Reel name, scene, notes | | ✅ |
| Title, description, keywords | | ✅ |
| Batch renaming with patterns | | ✅ |

**€3.99/month or €33/year.** Cancel whenever you like.

## Supported formats

MP4, MOV, AVI, MXF, MTS and the other common video containers.
Powered by [ExifTool](https://exiftool.org/).

## Where it fits

Clock Fix Pro is the step *before* ingest. With the clocks lined up,
[Ingest Pro](https://www.ingest-pro.com) can rebuild your multicam day as
a single timeline with the real time between takes.

## Install

Download the installer from [Releases](../../releases/latest) and run it.
Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit.

> Windows may warn about an unrecognised publisher on first run. The app
> is not code-signed yet.

